  {
   "code": "rate-is-last-movement-price",
   "detail": "14 holding(s) print a rate and a value that describe the holding's LAST DEPOSITORY MOVEMENT, not its balance — e.g. ABSL BAL ADV-GROWTH: 183499.511 held, rate 108.65, value 19937221.76, which is 183499.510 units, the quantity of that movement. So these carry their units and no market value; the rate and value are kept as `lastMovementRate` / `lastMovementValue`, a transaction price rather than a valuation. The value column sums to the printed Total Holding Valuation of Rs 273437881.06 to the rupee, so every row was read — and that total is a sum of last-movement values, not what the account is worth."
  }
